subject: docs(plans-and-prompts): reorganize knowledge base into category taxonomy

Reorganize docs/plans-and-prompts/ from a flat structure into 9 categories
(architecture, connections, security, ui-ux, operations, planning, research,
tracking, templates), each with its own README.md. All moves use git mv to
preserve history:

- plans/ -> planning/
- workflows/ -> operations/ (old workflows/README.md renamed to
  operations/TESTING.md; a fresh generic operations/README.md was written)
- prompts/ -> templates/
- decisions/, learnings/, meetings/ -> tracking/{decisions,learnings,meetings}/
- CHANGELOG.md, TASK-LOG.md (renamed TASKS.md), SESSION-HISTORY.md,
  SESSION-NARRATIVE.md -> tracking/

architecture/ and research/ were already correctly scoped and left in place.
temp/ (gitignored, no history, contains scratch/draft content) is
intentionally excluded from the migration.

New operating documents authored per category: ARCHITECTURE.md,
CONNECTIONS.md, SECURITY.md, UI-UX.md, OPERATIONS.md, VERSIONING.md,
RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md, WORK-ITEM-TEMPLATE.md, RESEARCH-NOTE-TEMPLATE.md,
tracking/DECISIONS.md, tracking/FINDINGS.md, tracking/CODE-CHANGES.md, and a
top-level GLOSSARY.md. Top-level README.md and AGENTS.md rewritten for the
new taxonomy, including the security rule (never commit real secrets/URLs/
personal data to this folder) and the distinction between this folder's
internal tracking/CHANGELOG.md and the repo-root user-facing CHANGELOG.md.

Repaired every stale relative-path cross-reference created by the moves
across research/, planning/, operations/, and tracking/ (including the two
large historical logs, SESSION-HISTORY.md and SESSION-NARRATIVE.md) so links
resolve correctly from each file's new location.

